    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1991-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Lining up the subtraction gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} &1{,}000{,}000{,}000{,}000 \\\\ &\\quad {}- 777{,}777{,}777{,}777 \\\\ &= 222{,}222{,}222{,}223. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nEquivalently, to climb from \\(777{,}777{,}777{,}777\\) up to \\(1{,}000{,}000{,}000{,}000\\) you add \\(3\\) in the units place and \\(2\\) in each of the other eleven places.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Think of the amount you must add to \\(777{,}777{,}777{,}777\\) to reach \\(1{,}000{,}000{,}000{,}000\\)",
        "Work from the right: the units digits must add to \\(10\\) with a carry, and every other column then adds to \\(10\\) with that carry"
      ],
